The default button takes the focus, and without this the message text did.

An NSAlert builds two text fields and makes both SELECTABLE, which is right: macOS alert text can be
selected. Neither is editable. But the panel had no initial first responder, so when it opened the
first selectable view in the key view loop became one, and a selectable field answers that by handing
out its field editor with the WHOLE STRING SELECTED.

So an alert came up with its message painted as selected text. Measured in Money Manager EX, behind
the words New Database: (178,214,255), which is exactly selectedTextBackgroundColor from the table,
while the informative line below it sat on the ordinary (237,237,237). One label looked highlighted
and the other did not, in the same panel.

macOS gives the focus to the DEFAULT BUTTON, which is why Return dismisses an alert. Both entry
points, runModal and beginSheetModalForWindow, now set it, next to the setDefaultButtonCell: that was
already there. Measured after: zero selection coloured pixels behind the message, black glyphs on
the panel background, and the OK button draws its focus ring.

Task #242. Gates: run-dts-batch, buck-bundled-patch-record-check, roster-sweep and roster-input.

--- a/AppKit/NSAlert.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSAlert.m
@@ -656,6 +656,7 @@
     [_window setStyleMask: NSDocModalWindowMask];
     [self layoutIfNeeded];
     [_window setDefaultButtonCell: [[_buttons objectAtIndex: 0] cell]];
+    [self _focusDefaultButton];
     _sheetDelegate = delegate;
     _sheetDidEnd = selector;
 
@@ -678,11 +679,28 @@
                        contextInfo: 0];
 }
 
+/*
+ * THE DEFAULT BUTTON TAKES THE FOCUS, and without this the message text did.
+ *
+ * Both text fields are selectable, which is what macOS alerts are, and the first selectable view in
+ * the key view loop becomes first responder when the panel opens. A selectable field answers that
+ * by handing out its field editor with the WHOLE STRING SELECTED, so the message came up painted in
+ * selectedTextBackgroundColor: measured at (178,214,255) behind New Database in Money Manager EX,
+ * while the informative text below it sat on the ordinary (237,237,237). Task #242.
+ *
+ * macOS focuses the default button instead, which is why Return dismisses an alert.
+ */
+- (void) _focusDefaultButton {
+    if ([_buttons count] > 0)
+        [_window setInitialFirstResponder: [_buttons objectAtIndex: 0]];
+}
+
 - (NSModalResponse) runModal {
     [_window setLevel: NSModalPanelWindowLevel];
     [_window setStyleMask: NSTitledWindowMask];
     [self layoutIfNeeded];
     [_window setDefaultButtonCell: [[_buttons objectAtIndex: 0] cell]];
+    [self _focusDefaultButton];
     return [NSApp runModalForWindow: _window];
 }
 
